<heading>dig - Create a box and connect to it.</heading>
<rule/>
<heading level="2">Usage</heading>
<pre>dig NAME
dig NAME --direction north
dig NAME --direction east --oneway
dig NAME --world NLP</pre>
<heading level="2">Description</heading>
<paragraph>Creates a new box and connects it to the current box. If a box with the given name already exists, only the connection is created. The box is created in the current world by default; use --world to create (or find) it in another world.</paragraph>
<paragraph>The direction is the orientation at the current box, given as a compass word or an angle in degrees (0° = east, counterclockwise). Connections are bidirectional by default; use --oneway to make one directional.</paragraph>
<heading level="2">Examples</heading>
<pre>dig Garden
  Create a box and connect to it.
dig Office --direction east
  Create a box with its endpoint on the east side.
dig Portals --world NLP
  Create a box in the NLP world and connect to it.</pre>
<heading level="2">See also</heading>
<paragraph>connect, enter, go, leave, look, place</paragraph>
